An older compiler might choke on new language features, but a new compiler =
will always work with old code.<br>
<br>
Compiler vendors may introduce their own language features as forks (and th=
ey are not considered standard C&#43;&#43;), but there is always a standard=
/&quot;strict&quot; mode that can be enabled. Most good features that compi=
lers introduce have been added to the official version,
